:Namespace flash_attention

⍝ FlashAttention is a good example of an algorithm in which we have a much 
⍝ nicer expression of the actual computation in plain APL, but the memory
⍝ and execution behaviors are not sufficient for our needs. 
⍝ 
⍝ In this case, we are going to do a tiling optimization to help make the 
⍝ attention algorithm more cache friendly. See the FlashAttention paper, 
⍝ Algorithm 1 for the pseudo-code that you are going to implement. 

⎕IO ⎕CT←0

⍝ We will use the following four cases to benchmark our code. These specify 
⍝ the values of N and d in our algorithm. 

cases←(16384 64)(32768 64)(8192 128)(16384 128)

⍝ The attention algorithm uses the following core data variables.

Q←⍬ ⋄ K←⍬ ⋄ V←⍬

⍝ Here is a naive attention algorithm expressed in simple APL, along with 
⍝ a simple L2 normalization function to check the results.

L2←{(0.5*⍨+⌿×⍨,⍵)-0.5*⍨×⌿⍺}
attn←{(fx÷[0]+/fx←*S-[0]⌈/S←Q+.×⍉K)+.×V}

⍝ Your job will be to implement Algorithm 1 from the paper above. Good luck!
⍝ Here's the basic skeleton:

flash_attn←{M←⍺ ⍝ Getting a block size, defaulting to 2*23

	∘∘∘ ⍝ The algorithm goes here!

	N d⍴O
}

⍝ And here's some code to run and benchmark the results! You'll call Run cn
⍝ where cn is the case index into the cases variable above that indicates 
⍝ which case you want to run. 

Run←{N d←⍵⊃cases ⋄ ⍺←⊢ ⋄ M←⍺⊣2*23
	Q K V∘←N d∘⍴¨1 1 1
	Gflops←((N*2)×(4×d)+5)÷2*30
	
	⎕←''
	⎕←'Running naive version...'
	
	start←24 60 60 1000⊥¯4↑⎕TS
	res←attn ⍬
	end←24 60 60 1000⊥¯4↑⎕TS
	⍝ ⎕←'Naive L2: ',⍕N d L2 res
	⎕←'Naive Attention time elapsed: ',(⍕time←(end-start)÷1000),'secs'
	⎕←(⍕d N),' Naive Attention throughput: ',(⍕Gflops÷time),' Gflops/sec'
		
	start←24 60 60 1000⊥¯4↑⎕TS
	res←M flash_attn ⍬
	end←24 60 60 1000⊥¯4↑⎕TS
	time←(end-start)÷1000
	⍝ ⎕←'Flash Attention L2: ',⍕N d L2 res
	⎕←'Flash Attention time elapsed: ',(⍕time),'secs'
	⎕←(⍕d N),' Flash Attention throughput: ',(⍕Gflops÷time),' Gflops/sec'
	
	1:shy←res
}

:EndNamespace